abstract: >-
  Python program, run from cron or a systemd timer, that checks websites and JSON endpoints and the
  expiry of their TLS certificates, keeps every outage as an incident with its start, end and
  duration in SQLite, and sends grouped alerts with escalating reminders and a message on
  recovery, each kind of message by the route one chooses (email, a command of one's own such as
  a chat client, or both), sending again what could not be delivered and falling back on a spare
  route when the mail cannot be sent. It recognises a flapping target, and writes daily, weekly
  and monthly summaries as an email table, a short message for a chat, or JSON for other
  programs. A shell watchdog beside it looks every five minutes for the signs of a crypto-miner
  or a backdoor on the server, reporting a busy process only when its load lasts, and sends its
  findings through the same channels.
